# CUBE script: Reusable TMs (OFF)
#
# ON means a TM is not used up when it teaches a move (it stays in the bag, like an HM); OFF means a TM is used up as in the normal game. OFF is how CUBE comes.
#
# What it does
#   A TM is used up when it teaches a move to a Pokemon (in the bag menu and in the move relearner's TM list), as in the normal game. TMs can be sold and tossed again.
#
# How to undo
#   Run CUBE_ReusableTMs_ON.hma, or press Ctrl+Z before you save.
#
# How to use
#   1. Open your CUBE ROM in HexManiacAdvance.
#   2. Drag this file onto HexManiacAdvance.
#   3. Look at the result, then save the ROM.
#   It works on a CUBE ROM that has this option (CUBE round 14f and later; Update CUBE brings an older one up to date).
#   On any other ROM the script stops with a message and changes nothing.
#
# What it writes
#   One byte of the table cube.scripts.config (byte 6 = 1 for on, 0 for off). Nothing else in the ROM changes; the items table is not touched.
#
.python
tab = editor.SelectedTab
if tab.Model.GetAddressFromAnchor(tab.CurrentChange, -1, 'cube.scripts.config') < 0:
  tab.RaiseError('No CUBE script table (cube.scripts.config): this is not a CUBE ROM, or it is a CUBE older than round 14 (older Apply CUBE). Nothing was changed.')
  tab.AbortScript()
.end

@cube.scripts.config+6 0

.python
editor.SelectedTab.RaiseMessage('CUBE: TMs are used up when they are taught (the normal game).')
.end
